<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stans is the capital of the Swiss canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidwalden">Nidwalden</a>, at the foot of the Stanserhorn south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a>. In 1481 the Diet of Stans, helped by the mediation of the hermit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niklaus-von-flue">Niklaus von Flüe</a>, settled a crisis that threatened to split the Confederacy. After the French massacre of 1798, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-heinrich-pestalozzi">Johann Heinrich Pestalozzi</a> ran an orphanage there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stans.jpg" alt="Stans" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scoutboy · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stans_rathaus_3_thm.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
